# Test the lab API (Fake WhatsApp client). Run the API first:
#   dotnet run --project src\WhatsAppLab.Api --urls http://localhost:5300
# Open this file in VS Code (REST Client) or Visual Studio and click "Send Request". Swagger: http://localhost:5300/swagger

@base = http://localhost:5300/api/whatsapp

### 1. Status (feature is Off by default)
GET {{base}}/status

### 2. Switch the feature on (limits: 100 per day, 1 second between messages)
PUT {{base}}/settings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isEnabled": true, "maxMessagesPerDay": 100, "minSecondsBetweenMessages": 1, "receiveEnabled": true }

### 3. Sync groups of the linked number, then list them
POST {{base}}/groups/sync

###
GET {{base}}/groups

### 4. Trigger by API: queue a message to a group (sent by the background worker)
POST {{base}}/messages
Content-Type: application/json

{ "groupName": "IT Batam", "body": "Test from the API" }

### 5. Scheduled: sent only when the time is due (UTC)
POST {{base}}/messages
Content-Type: application/json

{ "groupName": "IT Batam", "body": "Scheduled test", "scheduledFor": "2026-11-14T08:00:00Z" }

### 6. See the outbox (status 0 Pending, 1 Sent, 2 Failed)
GET {{base}}/messages

### 7. Recurring announcement (Hangfire), then run it now
POST {{base}}/announcements
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "daily-test", "groupName": "IT Batam", "body": "Daily announcement", "cron": "0 9 * * *" }

###
POST {{base}}/announcements/daily-test/run-now

### 8. Receive: simulate an incoming group message, then read what was recorded
POST {{base}}/fake/incoming
Content-Type: application/json

{ "groupName": "IT Batam", "sender": "Karen", "body": "Hello from a member" }

###
GET {{base}}/inbound

### 9. Failure test: the next send fails once, then is retried
POST {{base}}/fake/fail-next

### 10. What the fake client really "sent"
GET {{base}}/fake/sent
